```
Title: CMSTP App Paths Registry Key Modification
Author: Nik Seetharaman
Date: 2018-07-16
Level: high
Description: Detects modifications to the CMSTP App Paths registry key. This may indicate abuse of
# Microsoft Connection Manager Profile Installer (CMSTP) for arbitrary code execution or UAC bypass.
MITRE Tactic: Execution
Tags: attack.execution, attack.stealth, attack.t1218.003, attack.g0069, car.2019-04-001
Reference: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/master/rules/windows/registry/registry_event/registry_event_cmstp_execution_by_registry.yml
# False Positives:
#   - Legitimate CMSTP use (unlikely in modern enterprise environments)
```
TargetObject="*SOFTWARE\\Microsoft\\Windows\\CurrentVersion\\App Paths\\cmmgr32.exe\\*" NOT ((Details IN ("C:\\Windows\\System32\\cmcfg32.dll", "C:\\Windows\\SysWOW64\\cmcfg32.dll") TargetObject="*SOFTWARE\\Microsoft\\Windows\\CurrentVersion\\App Paths\\cmmgr32.exe\\CmstpExtensionDll") OR Details="(Empty)")